      "writtenOn": "2025-07-28T15:44:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Which call? In the case of direct recursion there\u0027s an obvious candidate, but for indirect recursion there\u0027s no single call or function that caused the recursion (it\u0027s a cycle in a call graph, so every node is responsible).\n\nWith some extra work would could definitely improve the diagnostic to show more details, including a full callstack that shows the whole call loop. I question how valuable it is to do this work though, given that I think these are pretty infrequently hit by Tint developers and probably not that hard to figure out what\u0027s going on once you\u0027ve been told that there is recursion.",
      "parentUuid": "8d93daa9_cb40e791",
      "revId": "5a41eaf96b56965724407e112fcae039b0ffec99",
